      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Inter Dominion placegetter NYACK (10) drew wide and was held up in the city last time but had put together a string of placings in strong company prior. Draws on the back row but has won two of three attempts here and will enjoy the class drop. NEPTUNITE (2) is a progressive three-year-old who took his perfect record at this circuit to seven when he came from the outside barrier and scored by 3 metres last time. Draws well so could match the older rivals. IMA BOXA (5) has returned to the Jake Stockton yard since a last-start third in the Regional Championship State Final in May having won the Metropolitan version earlier. Two-from-two at this circuit and distance and has been readied with two trials, winning the latest. Last-start winner DAY TWO (9) draws for a trail and deserves some respect.",
